  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>besselj</keyword>
  <short_description>Bessel function of the first kind.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>J = besselj(nu, Z)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>J = besselj(nu, Z, scale)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>nu</param_name>
      <param_description>order: real array.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>Z</param_name>
      <param_description>argument: real or complex array.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>scale</param_name>
      <param_description>0 (default) or 1 to return the scaled values.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>J</param_name>
      <param_description>Bessel function of the first kind.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>besselj(nu, Z)</b> computes the Bessel function of the first kind J for each element of NU and Z.</p>
    <p>Bessel functions are solutions of the Bessel differential equation:</p>
    <latex>z^2 \frac{d^2 w}{dz^2} + z \frac{dw}{dz} + (z^2 - \nu^2) w = 0</latex>
    <p><b>besselj(nu, Z, 1)</b> returns <b>besselj(nu, Z) .* exp(-abs(imag(Z)))</b>.</p>
    <p>NU and Z must have the same size, or one of them can be a scalar.</p>
    <p>The result is single when an input is single, and real when every imaginary part is zero.</p>
    <p>Values are computed with a C++ port of the Amos algorithms, for any real order and any complex argument.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography>D. E. Amos, Algorithm 644: A portable package for Bessel functions of a complex argument and nonnegative order, ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software, 12 (1986), pp. 265-273.</bibliography>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description></example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[J = besselj(0:3, 2.5)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description></example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[J = besselj(0.5, [1, -1, 2 + 3i])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="adv-cli"
      ><![CDATA[f = figure();
x = linspace(0, 20, 400);
[N, X] = meshgrid(0:3, x);
J = besselj(N, X);
plot(x, J);
grid on;
legend('J_0', 'J_1', 'J_2', 'J_3');
xlabel('x');]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img
        src="../../images/besselj.svg"
        align="middle"
        generate="true"
      />
    </example_item>
  </examples>
